@startuml single-tenant-auth
title Flujo Single-Tenant: Autenticación y Operación

actor "Admin" as Admin
participant "orch-cli" as CLI
participant "Orchestrator" as Orch
participant "Tenant Único\n(tenant-a)" as TA
participant "Peer 1\n(peer01)" as P1
participant "Peer 2\n(peer02)" as P2

== Provisioning del Tenant Único ==
Admin -> CLI : orch-cli user-create tenant-a --admin-token $ADMIN
CLI -> Orch : orch.user-create("tenant-a", admin_token)
Orch -> Orch : _issue_user_token("tenant-a")\ngenera u_<hex16>
Orch --> CLI : {user_id: "tenant-a", token: "u_abc..."}
CLI --> Admin : token guardado en peer.env (ORCH_TOKEN)

== Peer 1 obtiene JWT ==
P1 -> Orch : auth.login("tenant-a", "peer01", ORCH_TOKEN, scopes)
Orch -> Orch : _check_user_token\nvalida token del tenant
Orch --> P1 : {jwt, expires_at: 600s}

== Peer 1 se registra ==
P1 -> Orch : peer.register("peer01", pub_key, endpoint, jwt)
Orch -> Orch : _auth_from_token(jwt)\n→ user_id="tenant-a"
Orch -> Orch : rpc_peer_register\nuser_id="tenant-a" guardado en peer
Orch --> P1 : {peer_id, wg_ip=10.0.0.2, config_version}

== Peer 2 obtiene JWT y se registra ==
P2 -> Orch : auth.login("tenant-a", "peer02", ORCH_TOKEN, scopes)
Orch --> P2 : {jwt, expires_at: 600s}
P2 -> Orch : peer.register("peer02", pub_key, endpoint, jwt)
Orch -> Orch : rpc_peer_register\nmismo user_id="tenant-a"
Orch --> P2 : {peer_id, wg_ip=10.0.0.3, config_version}

== Acceso entre Peers (mismo tenant) ==
P1 -> Orch : peer.get("peer02", jwt_de_tenant_a)
Orch -> Orch : _auth_from_token(jwt)\n→ user_id="tenant-a"
Orch -> Orch : _enforce_tenant_for_peer("tenant-a", "peer02")
Orch -> Orch : peer.user_id == "tenant-a" ✓ coincide
Orch --> P1 : {peer_id: "peer02", wg_ip, endpoint, ...}

== Admin lista peers del tenant ==
Admin -> CLI : orch-cli peer-list --admin-token $ADMIN
CLI -> Orch : peer.list(admin_token)
Orch -> Orch : orch_check_admin_token\n(bypass multi-tenant, ve todo)
Orch --> CLI : {peers: {peer01: {...}, peer02: {...}}}
CLI --> Admin : lista completa (único tenant)

== Refresh de JWT (60s antes de expirar) ==
P1 -> Orch : auth.refresh(jwt, TTL)
Orch -> Orch : _jwt_decode(jwt)\nvalida exp, iss, aud
Orch --> P1 : {jwt_nuevo, expires_at: ...}

note over Orch
  **Sin aislamiento entre tenants** (sólo uno):
  - Todos los peers comparten user_id="tenant-a"
  - _enforce_tenant_for_peer siempre coincide → OK
  - No hay riesgo de cross-tenant forbidden (403)
  - JWT contiene user_id + scopes (igual que en multi-tenant)
  - Admin sigue teniendo bypass con admin_token
  - Refresh y revocación de JWT idénticos al modelo multi-tenant
end note

@enduml